      "text": "When dividing a polynomial \\( P(x) \\) by another polynomial \\( D(x) = 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\), the division algorithm states that:\n\\[ P(x) = (2x^2 - 7x + 18)Q(x) + R(x) \\]\nwhere \\( Q(x) \\) is the quotient and \\( R(x) \\) is the remainder. The degree of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) must be less than the degree of the divisor \\( D(x) \\). The degree of \\( D(x) \\) is 2.\n\nTherefore, the possible degrees of \\( R(x) \\) are 0 or 1 (since the remainder cannot be a constant unless the remainder polynomial is zero, which does not change the degree).\n\nHence, the possible degrees of the remainder are \\( 0 \\) and \\( 1 \\).\n\nThe final answer is \\( \\boxed{0, 1} \\).\n\nThe polynomial \\( P(x) \\) is such that \\( P(a) = k \\). Then \\( P(a + h) = k \\), and thus \\( D(x) | P(x) - k \\). Without the specific values, we cannot determine the exact degrees, but we know the degrees must be less than 2. \n\nTherefore, the possible degrees of the remainder are \\(\\boxed{0, 1}\\).",
