      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to consider the properties of polynomial division. According to the polynomial division algorithm, any polynomial \\( P(x) \\) when divided by a divisor polynomial \\( D(x) \\) can be expressed as:\n\\[ P(x) = Q(x) \\cdot D(x) + R(x), \\]\nwhere:\n- \\( P(x) \\) is the dividend,\n- \\( D(x) \\) is the divisor,\n- \\( Q(x) \\) is the quotient,\n- \\( R(x) \\) is the remainder.\n\nThe degree of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) must be less than the degree of the divisor \\( D(x) \\). Given that the divisor is \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\), we need to determine the degree of this divisor.\n\nThe degree of a polynomial is the highest power of \\( x \\) in the polynomial. Let's find the degree of \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\).\n\nThe polynomial \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\) has terms \\( 2x^2 \\), \\( -7x \\), and \\( 18 \\). The highest power of \\( x \\) in this polynomial is 2 (from the term \\( 2x^2 \\)). Therefore, the degree of \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\) is 2.\n\nSince the degree of the remainder must be less than the degree of the divisor, the possible degrees of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) are:\n\\[ 0, 1, \\]\n\\[ -2 \\text{ (but a remainder cannot have a negative degree in standard polynomial division)}. \\]\n\nThus, the possible degrees of the remainder are \\( 0 \\) and \\( 1 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0, 1}\n\\]",
